<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">ticks</ansi>

A <ansi fg="command">tick</ansi> is a repeating timer that fires one or more
commands automatically at a set interval while you are
connected through the web client.

<ansi fg="yellow">How it works:</ansi>

  While you're logged in through the web client, each
  enabled tick runs its commands every N seconds — hands-
  free, on a loop. Ticks pause when you disconnect; they
  resume the next time you log in with a capable client.

  Tick definitions save to your account and sync across
  sessions, so your timers are always ready when you
  return.

<ansi fg="yellow">Managing ticks:</ansi>

  Ticks are created and managed in the
  <ansi fg="command">Triggers &amp; Timers</ansi> panel — there is no typed
  command for them.

  <ansi fg="command">+ New</ansi>         Open the editor to create a tick.
  <ansi fg="command">Toggle</ansi>        Enable or disable a tick without deleting
                 it. Disabled ticks will not fire.
  <ansi fg="command">Left-click</ansi>    Fire the tick's commands right now, once.
  <ansi fg="command">Right-click</ansi>   Open the context menu to Edit, Duplicate,
                 or Remove a tick.

<ansi fg="yellow">Commands &amp; intervals:</ansi>

  A tick can run more than one command. Separate them with
  a semicolon — the same way macros work:

    <ansi fg="command">forage;rest</ansi>

  The shortest interval allowed is <ansi fg="command">1 second</ansi>. Most
  repeating tasks work well at 30–60 seconds or longer.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help macros</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help alias</ansi>
